    <div class="info-box">
      <strong>Rule for 14px button text (normal weight):</strong>
      AA requires ≥ 4.5:1. For each scale, the minimum step that passes on white is <strong>Step 50</strong> (Grey/Red/Green/Blue) or <strong>Step 50</strong> (Yellow). On dark (#080808), it's <strong>Step 40</strong> for chromatic scales and <strong>Step 40–50</strong> for greys.
      Steps marked ⚠ clear 4.5:1 only marginally — prefer one step darker (higher step number on white; lower on dark) for robust compliance across display variability.
      <br><br>
      <strong>Yellow exception:</strong> Yellow 20–30 appear bright but sit at low contrast on white. Always use Yellow 50+ for text on white. Yellow is best used as a background tint with dark (Step 70+) text on top.
    </div>
